      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jett: the default OVP threshold is 6V. (Please refer to the register VBUS_OVP_THR_CFG in the section 3.1.2 Port Controller Vendor-Defined Registers in our datasheet.)\nWe definitely can set it to 21V. However, I would like to confirm that where the TCPM common code handles the OVP event?\nIn our TCPC, if the OVP is detected, it will set the\nInternal_or_External_OVP_VBUS_Over_Voltage_Protection_Fault bit (B2) in FAULT_STATUS register to 1. I further checked the common code in TOT (c91a91b0f4), it seems that it doesn\u0027t handle the fault status register (and also fault bit (B9) in the ALERT register.) I think the OVP event will not be handled. Do I miss something?",
